.TH GROW 1 "2026-07-14" "GROW 0.1.21" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
grow \- Git Repository Oriented Web runtime command-line interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B grow
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B grow
loads a committed GROW application from a Git repository. Manifest,
static assets, and WebAssembly entry modules are read from the verified HEAD
tree, not from uncommitted working-tree files. Commands accept a repository
path or the name of an installed app.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B inspect \fIREPO-OR-APP\fR
Print the application name, manifest version, verified commit ID, runtime
entry configuration, requested permissions, and storage quota.
.TP
.B run \fIREPO-OR-APP\fR
Execute the WebAssembly runtime once with a GET request for / and print its
CGI-style response. For an installed app the install-time approval record is
enforced and the app's private storage directory is preopened as the
module's filesystem root with its quota enforced. A plain repository path
runs in dev mode: no approval check and no storage grant.
.TP
.B serve [--port \fIPORT\fR] \fIREPO-OR-APP\fR
Run the local HTTP daemon on 127.0.0.1. The default port is 7870. Approval
and storage handling match
.BR run .
.TP
.B install [--approve-capabilities] \fIREPO\fR
Register an app in the local registry: verified commit, manifest identity,
source path, requested capabilities, and an approval record.
.I REPO
is a local repository path or a
.BR file://
URL; other URL schemes are rejected. Cloned sources are kept in the registry
cache until the app is removed. Cloning spawns
.BR git-upload-pack ,
so a
.B git
binary must be available on the host. Apps declaring host capabilities
(network, camera, microphone, clipboard, notifications, or full filesystem)
require
.BR --approve-capabilities .
.TP
.B list
List installed apps with version, short commit, and source path.
.TP
.B remove \fIAPP\fR
Remove an installed app's registry metadata and storage, plus the cached
clone when the app was installed from a clone source. External source
repositories are never touched.
.SH APPROVAL
Before every run or serve of an installed app, the verified HEAD commit and
the install-time approval record are checked. If the repository moved since
install,
.B grow
fails with "run grow install again to re-verify"; if the app declares host
capabilities that were not approved, it fails with "reinstall with
--approve-capabilities". Approved capabilities are recorded but not yet
granted to modules.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print command help.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Print the GROW CLI version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .grow/manifest.toml
Application manifest read from the committed repository tree.
.TP
.I $GROW_HOME/apps/<name>/
Per-app registry directory holding metadata.toml and the private storage/
directory granted to the module. The registry root defaults to
$XDG_DATA_HOME/grow or ~/.local/share/grow when GROW_HOME is unset.
.TP
.I $GROW_HOME/cache/<name>/
Cached clone for an app installed from a clone source.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Non-zero on invalid repositories, manifests, runtime failures, approval
refusals, quota errors, or server startup errors.
